The crate is edition 2024, so `gen` is a RESERVED KEYWORD — never use `gen` as an identifier. Also edition 2024 requires explicit `unsafe {}` blocks even inside `unsafe fn`; prefer plain `fn` with inner `unsafe {}` blocks.

The C source is /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-WLUNsI/c_src/src/xxhash.c and header c_src/include/xxhash.h. It is compiled with XXH_NAMESPACE=LZ4_ so ALL exported symbols are prefixed `LZ4_`. Read the C source to confirm exact signatures and semantics before writing tests.

Exported symbols to cover (all must be called on BOTH libs and compared):
LZ4_XXH32, LZ4_XXH32_createState, LZ4_XXH32_freeState, LZ4_XXH32_reset, LZ4_XXH32_update, LZ4_XXH32_digest, LZ4_XXH32_copyState, LZ4_XXH32_canonicalFromHash, LZ4_XXH32_hashFromCanonical, LZ4_XXH64, LZ4_XXH64_createState, LZ4_XXH64_freeState, LZ4_XXH64_reset, LZ4_XXH64_update, LZ4_XXH64_digest, LZ4_XXH64_copyState, LZ4_XXH64_canonicalFromHash, LZ4_XXH64_hashFromCanonical, LZ4_XXH_versionNumber

Signatures (verify against the header): XXH32 returns u32 taking (*const u8, usize, u32 seed); XXH64 returns u64 taking (*const u8, usize, u64 seed); createState returns *mut u8; freeState/reset/update return i32 (XXH_errorcode: XXH_OK=0, XXH_ERROR=1); reset takes (*mut u8, seed); update takes (*mut u8, *const u8, usize); digest returns u32/u64 from (*mut u8); copyState takes (*mut u8 dst, *const u8 src); canonicalFromHash takes (*mut u8 dst_canonical, hash); hashFromCanonical takes (*const u8) -> hash.

Write these tests, each with MANY randomized inputs and a FIXED seed:
1. `oneshot_xxh32` / `oneshot_xxh64`: length sweep {0,1,2,3,4,5,7,8,9,15,16,17,31,32,33,63,64,65,127,128,255,256,1024,4096,10000} x all SHAPES x seeds {0, 1, 0xFFFFFFFF (and for 64-bit also large u64 seeds), plus several random seeds}. Compare return values.
2. `streaming_xxh32` / `streaming_xxh64`: createState/reset/update.../digest/freeState. Feed the same data with update chunk patterns: all-at-once, 1 byte at a time, and chunk sizes {3,15,16,17,31,32,33} and random chunk sizes. Assert the streaming digest matches between C and Rust AND equals the corresponding one-shot value from the same library.
3. `copy_state_xxh32` / `copy_state_xxh64`: after some updates, copyState into a second state, then continue feeding DIFFERENT data to original vs copy, and compare all digests between C and Rust.
4. `digest_is_non_destructive`: call digest twice and after further updates; compare.
5. `canonical_roundtrip_32` / `canonical_roundtrip_64`: canonicalFromHash on many random hash values, compare the raw canonical bytes between C and Rust (big-endian), then hashFromCanonical to round-trip; also feed arbitrary random canonical byte arrays to hashFromCanonical and compare.
6. `version_number`: compare LZ4_XXH_versionNumber().
7. `null_and_zero_len`: update with a NULL input pointer and len==0 (expect XXH_OK per xxhash.c) and NULL with len!=0 (expect XXH_ERROR per xxhash.c) — read the C at xxhash.c lines ~450-470 and ~910-930 to confirm the exact behavior, and assert C and Rust return the SAME code. Also one-shot XXH32/XXH64 with len==0 (pointer may be non-null). Only pass a NULL pointer with len!=0 if the C actually guards it — verify in the source first.

