[38;5;10mLZ4F_compressBound_internal[0m (lz4frame.c:398-399) does arithmetic straight on the enum fields: [38;5;10mBHSize + contentChecksumFlag * BFSize[0m. Every enumerator of these enums is non-negative, so the C compiler gives them an [1munsigned[22m underlying type — I verified this directly rather than assuming it:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mc
[0m[38;5;10m(LZ4F_contentChecksum_t)-1 < 0   →  false   // unsigned
[0m[0m[0m
