So C reads [38;5;10m-1[0m as [38;5;10m4294967295[0m and zero-extends; the Rust declared the fields [38;5;10mc_int[0m and sign-extended. Fixed in [38;5;10msrc/lz4frame.rs[0m by declaring the five [38;5;10mLZ4F_frameInfo_t[0m enum fields ([38;5;10mblockSizeID[0m, [38;5;10mblockMode[0m, [38;5;10mcontentChecksumFlag[0m, [38;5;10mframeType[0m, [38;5;10mblockChecksumFlag[0m) plus their constants and helper signatures as [38;5;10mc_uint[0m. [38;5;10mc_int[0m→[38;5;10mc_uint[0m is ABI-identical for parameter passing, so no exported signature changed — only the arithmetic semantics. This is exactly the out-of-range-enum class the task flagged as invisible to happy-path tests.[0m[0m
